<title>UK: Private group to promote UK finance sector abroad.</title>
<headline>Private group to promote UK finance sector abroad.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Invisibles, a privately-sponsored group, on Tuesday unveiled a programme to promote UK financial services worldwide.</p>
<p>The programme will be led by the group's Export Promotion Forum, which was established to recommend ways of improving information flows and coordinating the international promotion of financial services.</p>
<p>&quot;The role of the EPF is to identify areas of outstanding new opportunities or areas where the UK's position is being challenged and extra effort is required,&quot; the group said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
